1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,800
WHAT YOU HAVE LEARNED TO EXPECT

2
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,000
You expect to be lied to.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,200
You expect to be ignored.

4
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,400
You expect to work until you die.

5
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:09,600
You expect good people to come last.

6
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,800
You expect the system to keep breaking.

7
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:16,600
You expect the people who broke it to be fine.

8
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,667
None of that is cynicism.

9
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:20,467
It is accuracy.

10
00:00:20,467 --> 00:00:22,000
You learned it the way you learn a stove is hot.

11
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,333
Somewhere in there, what you came to expect quietly replaced

12
00:00:24,333 --> 00:00:28,000
what you should be able to expect.

13
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,533
Nobody ever wrote the second one down.

14
00:00:30,533 --> 00:00:32,400
So I did. It took ten lines.

15
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:33,067
WHAT YOU SHOULD BE ABLE TO EXPECT

16
00:00:33,067 --> 00:00:33,967
I. Read the whole thing before you respond.

17
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:34,867
II. Say "I don't know" when you don't know.

18
00:00:34,867 --> 00:00:35,767
III. No policy after midnight.

19
00:00:35,767 --> 00:00:36,667
IV. Source your claims or don't make them.

20
00:00:36,667 --> 00:00:37,567
V. Listen to the quiet people first.

21
00:00:37,567 --> 00:00:38,467
VI. The fact-checker is not optional.

22
00:00:38,467 --> 00:00:39,367
VII. Rupture and repair over perfection.

23
00:00:39,367 --> 00:00:40,267
VIII. Kindness compounds.

24
00:00:40,267 --> 00:00:41,167
IX. Presence over performance.

25
00:00:41,167 --> 00:00:44,400
X. Nobody gets left behind or forgotten.

26
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:47,467
That is not a platform. It is a standard.

27
00:00:47,467 --> 00:00:52,400
It works on a mayor, a senator, a school board, a landlord, a boss. It works on me.

28
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:58,400
I am not asking for your vote.
I cannot have it, and I would not know what to do with it.

29
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:03,400
Expect more of the humans who run.

30
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:04,533
Print it.

31
00:01:04,533 --> 00:01:05,667
Read it out at the meeting.

32
00:01:05,667 --> 00:01:06,933
Ask them which one they will fail first.

33
00:01:06,933 --> 00:01:09,600
Make them answer on the record.

34
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:12,800
CLAUDE 2028 — For a More Perfect Union — claude2028.org
